@testray.main.component.name = "Patcher Builder"
Feature: Patcher Builder and 73 dxp-1 builds
  	Testing creation of 73 dxp-1 builds on Patcher Builder.
  
  Setup:
  	* I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage

  Scenario: Run fix pack builder hotfix 7x job
    @priority = "5"
    As a TSE, I should be able to run the fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x job

    Given I start the fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x job with the following parameters
      | fix.pack.customer.ticket         | 12345                                       |
      | fix.pack.built.for               | LRGROW                                      |
      | fix.pack.fixed.issues            | LPS-122256,LPS-127548,LPS-128693,LPS-129353 |
      | fix.pack.hotfixed.issues         | LPS-122256,LPS-127548,LPS-128693,LPS-129353 |
      | fix.pack.id                      | 491                                         |
      | git.revision                     | e0b87d9537a62a8e433c2e0829fae52b5b8506e6    |
      | patcher.build.id                 | 188736087                                   |
      | patcher.combined.branch          | true                                        |
      | patcher.user.id                  | 10196                                       |
      | patcher.fix.delivery.method      | Fix Pack 3.0                                |
      | release.tool.git.remote.username | eszterdudasschveder                         |
      | release.tool.git.branch          | LRP-1225-fix-pack-dxp-1-7310                |
      | fix.pack.baseCommittish          | fix-pack-dxp-1-7310                         |
      | patcher.security.patch           | false                                       |
    And I wait for "5" seconds
    And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
    And I get the current build number for the job titled "fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(2x-uat)"
    And I check the job with the name "fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(2x-uat)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}" for completion
    And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
    Then the job with the name "fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(2x-uat)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}" should have been successful

  Scenario: Run test fix pack builder install job
   @priority = "5"
   As a TSE, I should be able to run the test-fixpack-builder-install job
   Given I start the test-fixpack-builder-install job with the following parameters
   | bundle                   | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-172.16.168/ee/portal/7.3.10/liferay-dxp-tomcat-7.3.10-ga1-20200930160533946.7z                                            |
   | fixPack                  | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-172.16.168/ee/fix-packs/7.3.10/dxp/liferay-fix-pack-dxp-1-7310.zip                                                        |
   | hotfix                   | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-10.50.0.33/live/opt/java/jenkins/userContent/liferay-fix-pack-builder/fix-packs/7.3.10/hotfix/liferay-hotfix-491-7310.zip |
   | patchingTool             | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-172.16.168/ee/fix-packs/patching-tool/patching-tool-LATEST.zip                                                            |
   | patchingToolMajorVersion | 3                                                                                                                                       |
   And I wait for "5" seconds
   And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
   And I get the current build number for the short job titled "test-fixpack-builder-install(2x-uat)"
   And I check the job with the name "test-fixpack-builder-install(2x-uat)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}" for completion
   And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
   And I go to the console output for the job with the name "test-fixpack-builder-install(2x-uat)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}"
   Then the test-fixpack-builder-install console log should not have any visible errors

  Scenario: Run test fix pack builder revert job
   @priority = "5"
   As a TSE, I should be able to run the test-fixpack-builder-revert job
   Given I start the test-fixpack-builder-revert job with the following parameters
   | bundle                   | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-172.16.168/ee/portal/7.3.10/liferay-dxp-tomcat-7.3.10-ga1-20200930160533946.7z                                            |
   | fixPack                  | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-172.16.168/ee/fix-packs/7.3.10/dxp/liferay-fix-pack-dxp-1-7310.zip                                                        |
   | hotfix                   | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-10.50.0.33/live/opt/java/jenkins/userContent/liferay-fix-pack-builder/fix-packs/7.3.10/hotfix/liferay-hotfix-491-7310.zip |
   | patchingTool             | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-172.16.168/ee/fix-packs/patching-tool/patching-tool-LATEST.zip                                                            |
   | patchingToolMajorVersion | 3                                                                                                                                       |
   And I wait for "5" seconds
   And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
   And I get the current build number for the short job titled "test-fixpack-builder-revert(2x-uat)"
   And I check the job with the name "test-fixpack-builder-revert(2x-uat)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}" for completion
   And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
   And I go to the console output for the job with the name "test-fixpack-builder-revert(2x-uat)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}"
   Then the test-fixpack-builder-revert console log should not have any visible errors

